    "body": "I have not looked into the port issue, but FWIW I'm pretty sure you can do away with the file host state in the standard fairly easily. Just parse them as special URLs and enforce that the authority does not have credentials later. Then you can handle whatever is decided about the port there too. You need to go back to using nulls for empty user/pass though, which I think I saw somewhere has changed before. \r\n\r\nRight now the host parser (which is called from the file host state) raises an error on `:` and `@`, so it just changes where the error is raised.",
